# UI/UX Patterns and Best Practices

## Modal and Dialog Layout

When creating modals with dynamic content (tables, lists, forms that can grow):

### Required Pattern

```tsx
<DialogContent className="max-w-3xl max-h-[90vh] overflow-hidden flex flex-col">
  <DialogHeader className="shrink-0">
    {/* Header - fixed at top */}
  </DialogHeader>

  <div className="flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto py-4">
    {/* Scrollable content area */}
  </div>

  <DialogFooter className="shrink-0">
    {/* Footer with buttons - always visible */}
  </DialogFooter>
</DialogContent>
```

### Key CSS Classes

- `flex flex-col` on DialogContent - enables flex layout
- `shrink-0` on header/footer - prevents shrinking
- `flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto` on content - allows scrolling
- `max-h-[90vh]` - prevents modal from exceeding viewport

### Why This Matters

Without proper layout, action buttons can be pushed off-screen when content grows, making the modal unusable.

## Image Display

### Always Validate URLs

```tsx
// Before rendering images, check for valid URLs
if (!imageUrl) {
  console.warn(`Missing image URL for ${itemId}`)
  return <Placeholder />
}
return <img src={imageUrl} alt={altText} />
```

### API Data Transformation

When converting API responses to UI models:

```tsx
export function apiToUIModel(data: APIData): UIModel {
  // Check required fields
  if (!data.imageUrl) {
    console.warn(`Item ${data.id} has no image URL`)
    return {
      id: data.id,
      url: '', // Empty string prevents src="" errors
      name: `Item ${data.id.slice(0, 8)}`,
    }
  }
  
  return {
    id: data.id,
    url: data.imageUrl,
    name: data.name || `Item ${data.id.slice(0, 8)}`,
  }
}
```

## Statistics and Counts

### Fetch Related Data Separately

Don't assume parent entities contain child counts. Fetch them explicitly:

```tsx
function EntityCard({ entity }: Props) {
  // Fetch related count
  const { data: childCount = 0 } = useEntityChildCount(entity.id)
  
  return (
    <Card>
      <span>{childCount} items</span>
    </Card>
  )
}
```

### Create Dedicated Hooks

```tsx
// In hooks.ts
export function useEntityChildCount(entityId: string | undefined) {
  return useQuery({
    queryKey: ['entity-child-count', entityId],
    queryFn: async () => {
      if (!entityId) return 0
      const children = await getChildren({ entityId })
      return children.length
    },
    enabled: !!entityId,
    staleTime: 60 * 1000,
  })
}
```

## Navigation Patterns

### Provide View Mode Toggles

When users might want to see data from different perspectives:

```tsx
function HubPage() {
  const [viewMode, setViewMode] = useState<'primary' | 'secondary'>('primary')
  
  return (
    <>
      <ViewToggle value={viewMode} onChange={setViewMode} />
      {viewMode === 'primary' ? <PrimaryView /> : <SecondaryView />}
    </>
  )
}
```

### Consider User Workflows

- What do users want to see first?
- What's the most common action?
- How do users navigate between related entities?

## Error Prevention Checklist

Before submitting UI code, verify:

- [ ] Modals with dynamic content have proper scroll handling
- [ ] Image URLs are validated before rendering
- [ ] API data transformations handle null/undefined
- [ ] Statistics are fetched, not assumed
- [ ] Loading states are shown while data loads
- [ ] Zero values are displayed correctly (not hidden)
- [ ] Navigation provides appropriate context
